   "fen": "r3r1k1/pp1n1ppp/2pq4/5b2/3Pp3/4P2P/PP1QBPPN/R3R1K1 b - - 1 15",
   "line": [
    "Nh2"
   ],
   "spoken": "There's a choice of approaches, and the positional one is to route a knight to d5 — a semi-outpost in the heart of the board. Resist the central break, which would only open lines for the opponent; keeping the centre closed is where the advantage lives.",
   "kind": "plan"
