   "line": [
    "Nd5"
   ],
   "spoken": "What is the centralised knight actually doing? Nothing specific — and that's fine. It occupies a central square, radiates control across the board, prevents the opponent's pawn expansion, and stands ready to spring to f4. Think about what a piece does, but don't box yourself in by demanding a single concrete task.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 33,
   "t": 733.5,
   "fen": "r3r1k1/pp3ppp/2pq4/3n1b2/3Pp3/P3P2P/1P1QBPPN/R1R3K1 b - - 0 17",
