   "fen": "r5k1/1p3ppp/2pqr3/p2n1b2/3Pp3/P3P2P/1PRQBPPN/R5K1 w - - 2 19",
   "line": [
    "Re6"
   ],
   "spoken": "There's a way to prevent the pawn break for good — a pawn to a4, so that any advance is met by a capture that hangs a rook. No rush to play it, though, since the break isn't yet a threat; first swing a rook toward the kingside, and keep the freeze in reserve.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 37,
   "t": 838,
   "fen": "r5k1/1p3ppp/2pqr3/p2n1b2/3Pp1B1/P3P2P/1PRQ1PPN/R5K1 b - - 3 19",
