   "line": [
    "f6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Pushing the enemy knight back takes real care — the immediate pawn thrust would only hand it a counter-outpost. So play the shielding pawn first to shut off that square, then the rook-pawn to chase the knight into the corner, and only then advance the f-pawn to blow the position open. One pawn stops the knight, the other does the pushing.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
