   "line": [
    "a4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The traditional plan is to prepare the pawn break with a rook behind it. Toss in the queenside freeze first so the opponent gets no counterplay — there's never a formula for how much a wing pawn is worth, but denying counterchances before attacking is the safe order.",
   "kind": "plan"
